tomorrow is president's day 45  individuals have held that office it's  been estimated that 545  million people have lived in this  country since we became a country and  yet only 45 men for now  have ever been called president  what do you think when you reflect on  those 45 men how many do you think  did a good job  what are your expectations for  a president do we want the person who is  best on policy the person most likely to  find consensus or the most persuasive  do we want someone we can relate to or  someone who appears larger than life do  we want a moral leader a business mind a  great public speaker  do we want a president who tells us what  we want to hear or one who tells us the  truth even if it's not what we want to  hear  there is some consensus that we like  george washington probably the same with  john adams and thomas and jefferson i've  always admired abraham lincoln because  of all he overcame the failures the  self-doubt all of which he overcame to  lead us during the most divisive time in  our country's history he seemed humble  like he took the job seriously but not  himself  i liked ronald reagan because he was  hopeful and like lincoln he experienced  defeat in life  but he came back to become one of our  most beloved presidents  my grandmother like franklin roosevelt  she was a very conservative person and  roosevelt did some very not conservative  things but she liked him  maybe we want a president we can like  america still mourns what could have  been with john f kennedy that was a loss  from which perhaps we will never recover  in the course of my lifetime only two  presidents have received more than 55  percent of the vote only two that i can  find  and yet five were elected president with  less than 50 percent of the popular vote  think about that we have not had a  consensus leader in 50 years  there have been more impeachments in my  lifetime than landslide presidential  winners so on the day we set aside to  honor presidents perhaps it's wise for  us to ask are the expectations we have  for our presidents reasonable to the  right kind of women and men seek that  office is it possible to succeed in any  office when half the people didn't want  you there in the first place  how do we even judge the success  of a president and what would it take to  find someone that perhaps  75 percent of us could rally around what  would it take to find a woman or a man  who generated real consensus someone  with a real mandate to lead this country  if we are an exceptional country  shouldn't we have exceptional leaders so  how many of our presidents would you  describe as exceptional  it may be the best way to spend  president's day is to reflect on  precisely what it is we are looking for  in a president  does the process of seeking that office  encourage the caliber  of women and men you most want to run  and serve  i guess the thing i ask myself on this  president's day is a simple but  uncomfortable question  if we struggle to find presidents we  like and respect  does that say more about us or them  there's a difference between being a  president and being a leader  and maybe the process the political  environment and the media have made it  such that the real leaders do not want  this job so we're left with those who  covet the title while we as a nation are  left to covet real leaders  i don't even know if george washington  thomas jefferson abraham lincoln or  ronald reagan would seek the job today  or if they would be nominated for the  job today or if they would win the job  today  i do know this great people should have  great leaders and if those great leaders  aren't even running  then we should ask why not  i'm steve ducey i'm brian kilny and i'm  ainsley earhardt and click here to  subscribe to the fox news youtube page  to catch our hottest interviews and most  compelling analysis
 

